    <DataNode elementId="AT1G65520-MONOMER" textLabel="Enoyl-CoA delta isomerase 1, peroxisomal" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O04469" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">There are three genes in the Arabidopsis genome encoding delta3-delta2-enoyl-CoA isomerase. Functional complementation experiment of a yeast mutant indicated all three genes are functional. In vitro enzyme assay also confirmed activity of ECI2 and ECI3. However, unlike ECI1 and ECI2 which are located in the peroxisome, ECI3 is located in the cytosol, not a location where fatty acid degradation occurs. It was speculated that ECI3 may still function in the cis/trans isomerization of similar double bonds of cytosolic metabolites.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G65520-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G65520.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="O04469" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="Delta(3),Delta(2)-enoyl CoA isomerase 1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="AtECI1" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33196, RXN-10753" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G65520.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G65520" />
